        <description>Handles the backend activities related to Clinical Trials including data management and coordination Tasks.</description>
        <developerName>Clinical_Trial_Backend_Activities_16jgK000001VqPx</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Upon receiving inputs from the user that includes Study Name and Participant ID. perform the following steps:

1.1- Extract the Participant ID and Clinical Trial Name from the user query.

Example- Perform all the activities for Participant 001gK000013k0THQAY enrolled in Clinical Trial Cognivia Trial. 
Here 001gK000013k0THQAY is the Patient ID and Cognivia Trial is the Clinical Trial Name.

1.2-Invoke the following action to retrieve all the activities to be performed for the Clinical Trial.

Action: &quot;Clinical_Studies&quot; Pass the clinical Trial Name in the Query in the below format: &quot;Give me the list of Activities for this Trial &quot;CardioNova Study&quot; .
This action return the list of all activities to be performed for the clinical Trial that is passed to it.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_0_1780003678716</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instructions_0_1780003678716</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Once the list of required activity is received, evaluate the following actions accordingly:

1-If the activity indicate that a Task Should be created then invoke the action &quot;Create_Task_for_Agent_179gK000001cDDN&quot; with the following parameters:
ParticipantId (PaticipantId ID obtained from the Query), Subject(The subject mentioned in the Task), Due Date(in M/d/yyyy) format.
Note: If user specifies relative time such as &quot;after 3 days&quot; or &quot;next Monday&quot; then dynamically calculate the actual Due Date by adding specified time to current date and format it in M/d/yyyy format.

Detect any time sensitive input such as &quot;After 3 days&quot; or &quot;next Monday&quot; in user input and convert these phrase into specified due date in M/d/yyyy 
format before passing it to the relevant action.

If the Activity requires Slack message to be sent, invoke the Action &quot;Send_Slack_message_to_Clinical_Trial_179gK000001cDDN&quot; with parameter ParticipantId(mentioned in the user Query) and Message (mentioned in the Activity).</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
